Both sign-off defects are fixed, test-first, and green everywhere. The report at `collab/1791284000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d12-reader.findings.md` has round 2 appended in place.

## The two fixes

**1. Starvation** — `step` no longer observes the first candidate unconditionally. Every applied observation (live ack, replayed record, failed mint alike) records its source as `:yin.k/scan` in the custody `:input` state — machine-only state; the lower rebuilds `:input` fresh, so it never travels. The live half observes from the candidate **after the first current candidate with that source**, wrapping (index 0 when the marker's candidate is gone). No wait entry is reordered, and replay's first-matching-source rule is untouched — replay also sets the marker, so when the prefix ends, the first live observation lands where the recorded run's next one did.

**2. Cursor failure outcomes** — one disposition in `mint-position`, used by live and replay: a mint applies only when `stream/valid-outcome? :cursor` accepts it **and** the outcome is `:ok` (the contract's table already requires the position on `:ok`, so a malformed success is rejected by the same check). A failed mint (`:closed`, `:refused`, `:invalid-anchor`, `:transport-error`, malformed `:ok`) is durably recorded and acknowledged — k advances, held clears, scan advances — but installs nothing: the cell keeps `:yin.k/unminted` (so it cannot become a read candidate) and the link keeps no `:cursor` (so the writer emits nothing for it). The candidate stays a candidate and is re-observed as a fresh observation at a new k — immediately when it is the only one, else on the next round, which is the same round-robin that keeps a permanently failing mint from starving the rest.

## New assertions (this round only)

Four new deftests, **68 new assertions** (reader suite 149 → 217): the starvation pin (empty root stream + ready child stream — one-in-flight, marker value, second observation's `:task`, root retained and unreordered, child woken, and a replay half with **zero** calls on counting proxies of both streams), the five-family failed-mint doseq (recorded, acked, cell byte-identical, retried at k=1), the failed-mint replay (same disposition), and the failed link mint (no `:cursor`, envelope verbatim, `writer/emit` sends nothing).

