The r2 refinement is fixed and green everywhere. The report has round 3 appended in place at `collab/1791284000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d12-reader.findings.md`.

## The fix

Confirmed the defect exactly as quoted: round 2's `scan-start` advanced past the *first candidate* matching the saved source, so with two waiters sharing one cursor — equal sources, and a blocked read leaves both unchanged — live re-entered the same group (selecting the second alias) while replay's first-match selected the first, and a blocked alias pair recaptured the scan forever.

The change is confined to `scan-start` (+ a `distinct-sources` helper): the candidates' distinct sources, compared by content, form the scan's groups in canonical candidate order; the marker names a group; the live half observes from the **first candidate of the next distinct group**, wrapping. An alias group's turn is one observation, and within the selected group the first candidate in canonical order is always taken — the same candidate replay's first-matching-source selects for that group's source, so live and replay now wake identical continuations. Replay itself is untouched. Equal-source mint candidates (two unminted cells on one stream share one `:cursor` source) are one group like any other: first cell by `:seq` mints first; a failed first mint moves the scan to the next distinct group, not to the second cell; the group's next turn retries the first cell.

## New assertions (this round only)

Three deftests, **30 new assertions** (217 → 247): the alias-group test (distinct child stream progresses after the alias group's one acknowledged observation; both aliases parked, unreordered, cell unadvanced; rotation returns to the group's turn), the blocked-then-successful test (live and replay both wake `:k1` and leave `:k2` parked — the continuation-identity proof), and the mint-group test (both legs: ordered mints with the distinct reader between them, and the scripted `:closed` leg where the second observation goes to the distinct stream while both cells stay unminted and the retry targets the first cell).

